    turnFlow: '1. : The player with the lowest double (excluding ) leads that double to start the first round. After the first round, the loser of the previous round leads and must lead a double other than . 2. : The first double played is the spinner for the round. The first four plays must be on the four sides of the spinner, starting all four arms of the cross before any arm can be extended further. 3. : To place a regular tile, the end of the arm where it is played and the adjacent end of the played tile must total exactly 7. Valid pairs are: 1-6, 2-5, and 3-4. 4. : The four special tiles , , , and  can be played on any end without regard to the Rule of Seven. 5. : A player can choose to draw as many tiles as desired on their turn, but must leave at least 2 tiles in the boneyard. A player with no play must continue drawing until they find a playable tile or the boneyard is reduced to 2 tiles.',
